text:
tess: Noticed a weird edge with the Node sample app SSE path. If auth rotates while a large chunk is mid-flight and the client reconnects quickly, the parser occasionally stitches fragments in the wrong order and we get two closing tokens. Repro below.

omar: Minimal repro? Browser too?

tess: Node-only so far. Quick repro script:
````
// reconnect-drift.js
const {EventSource} = require('eventsource');
function spin(url){
  let i=0;
  const run = () => {
    const es = new EventSource(url);
    setTimeout(()=> es.close(), 90);
    setTimeout(()=> { if(++i<600) run(); }, 120 + Math.random()*80);
  }
  run();
}
spin(process.env.URL);
````
Logs show: fragment M (partial) arrives, auth refresh triggers reconnect, new conn emits N, then tail of M arrives -> parser emits N then M-tail -> malformed payload / duplicate final.

cleo: Could be parser swap without draining old socket. Did you try the SDK "holdUntilDelimiter" option?

tess: Tried holding until delimiter; lowers freq but doesn't eliminate because some servers don't flush delimiters at auth rotate.

omar: Short-term cheap fix: server can include a monotonic "x-chunk-seq" header per chunk and client drops chunks with seq <= lastSeen when it detects reconnect. No protocol break if feature-flagged.

cleo: Another mitigation: client waits a short drain window (configurable) before switching parsers when reconnecting, but that risks a slight latency blip.

sdk-bot: Filed RED-8008: "node sampleapp: reconnect drift -> SSE fragment reorder" with logs and repro.

ops-bot: Infra note: this gets worse with TCP reordering or lingering sockets; adding guidance to runbook.

tess: I'll prototype a small feature-flagged patch that implements seq-drop and an optional drainWindowMs in the sampleapp, plus an e2e that randomizes auth rotate time. Dropping the repro into devex/sampleapp/repro/reconnect-drift.js. Assigning @omar and @cleo for review.

omar: Sounds good. Please include a unit test simulating tail arrival after parser swap. I can add a lib-level test once the PR lands.

cleo: Long-term: parser should support reassembly across reconnects when resume token present; needs server support for per-fragment ids. We'll track in RED-8008.

tess: Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
